{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0217"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/theatre","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__theatre.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",554],["+","Not every landmark of those years came from the big names. The rock musical “Hair”, which opened at Joseph Papp's Public Theater off-Broadway on 17 October 1967 and moved to Broadway in April 1968, had book and lyrics by Gerome Ragni and James Rado, but its music – “Aquarius”, “Let the Sunshine In” – was written by the Canadian composer Galt MacDermot (1928–2018), a classically trained pianist from Montreal. Unlike “Cats” or “The Phantom of the Opera”, it owes nothing to Andrew Lloyd Webber, though it opened the way for the rock operas he would soon write.\n\n"],["=",402],["+","Galt MacDermot | Hair |\n| "],["=",48],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",60]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",510],["+","Nicht jeder Meilenstein jener Jahre stammte von den großen Namen. Das Rockmusical „Hair“, am 17. Oktober 1967 Off-Broadway in Joseph Papps Public Theater uraufgeführt und im April 1968 an den Broadway übernommen, hatte Buch und Texte von Gerome Ragni und James Rado, doch seine Musik – „Aquarius“, „Let the Sunshine In“ – schrieb der kanadische Komponist Galt MacDermot (1928–2018), ein klassisch ausgebildeter Pianist aus Montreal. Anders als „Cats“ oder „Das Phantom der Oper“ verdankt es Andrew Lloyd Webber nichts, bereitete aber den Weg für die Rockopern, die er bald schreiben sollte.\n\n"],["=",382],["+","Galt MacDermot | Hair |\n| "],["=",48],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",56]]}]},
